{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And you shall make for it.</b> For the table, <b>a frame (misgeret)</b> — a thing that closes in and surrounds. <b>A handbreadth (tefah)</b> — a handbreadth in height, all around, at the edge of the table, so that the bread would not fall." "<b>And you shall make a crown of gold for its frame.</b> If the frame was of wood, its crown was like a half-reed, hollow, to cover the frame from above and on its two sides. Thus all the wood in the table was overlaid with gold. And a proof for this: there were two crowns, as it is written in the section of ויקהל, 'and he made for it a crown of gold round about,' and it is written, 'and he made a crown of gold for its frame.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:27.340321361Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}